* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary

# The offline build is a byte-exact artefact, not source.
#
# CI proves it is current by rebuilding and diffing, which only works if git
# stores exactly what the build wrote. Left alone, git would normalise line
# endings on the way in and hand them back differently on a Windows checkout —
# so the check would fail for everyone on Windows and nobody on Linux, which is
# the worst possible way for it to be wrong.
offline/** -text
